Sir,

The matter pertains to an unjustified long delay of more than 30 years in the payment of terminal benefits / service dues that have been pending with CMO Bulandahar since 1992. Thus, the matter concerns human rights violations against this elderly, widowed, and ailing senior citizen. Despite this, officials are unconcerned with the mental agony and financial harassment of this widow and 74-year-old woman.

My previous complaints, Nos. 4001422203942, 40014223000138, and 40014223001780, had also been closed by the CMO Bulandhar on December 30, 2022, January 16, 2023, and February 4, 2023, respectively. Closure was without any redress, merely the GPF Passbook was asked for.&#160;

This is the scenario when it was immediately informed in response to the closure of first complaint No. 4001422203942 that the GPF Passbook was not provided.&#160;

The honourable Chief Minister of the Government of Uttar Pradesh notified and created this Jansunwai Samadhan portal for hassle-free redressal of grievances, however, the objective of the portal is being defied in the aforesaid manner.

I reiterate the following irrefutable facts:

1) I rendered services as an ANM from 1980 to 1992 under the jurisdiction of the CMO Bulandhar, and my date of birth is 02.06.1949.

2) Time and again, it has been informed to the CMO Bulandahar that the GPF Passbook was not provided and hence could not be furnished. However, three complaints were closed instead of providing the GPF passbook or statement and redressing the grievance.

3) Kindly get released the GPF, gratuity, leave encashment, insurance, pension, and other service benefit payments under your esteemed supervision.

Competent authority intervention in the matter is sought, and it will be much appreciated if it enables me to obtain these benefits in my old and ailing age, before my death.

I hope this request of mine will get your full attention.&#160;

Thanks and regards,&#160;


Smt. Santhamma Nair,
